From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 03:45:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/44] qwen27: a narrow tape beside the streams, and the
 window seam it measures

A windowed model's state is streams-wide, so one tape cannot hold both it and a
boundary plane one layer wide. Taps grows a second tape at hidden width and the
stage hook records both, which finally makes the window's own sub-seams
measurable: the branch a window layer's sublayer runs on, and the residual its
router read.

Both together must cover the requested planes, since a run may ask for either
tape alone; a loop visits a physical layer twice and the narrow tape keeps the
first visit as the seam.

Measured with it: the golden's two streams at enter are identical (max diff
0.0), i.e. the expand, and after the fold staging fix the engine's are identical
too. The fold's content is still wrong by ~6 against the layer-3 residual, which
is the next thing to fix.
